WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.320
- And we found this story on vogue.com

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.130
about Alyssa Bertrand.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:09.210
And she's a mom of six who
upcycles thrift store finds.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.620
And Alyssa, Alissa, excuse me,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.320
takes clothes, bedsheets,
tablecloths, and curtains

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.550
and turns them into insanely
cool children's clothing.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.490
And then she posts it all
on her Instagram account,

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.090
Jabellafleur, that's French for flower.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.090
And I am a lifelong
vintage store enthusiast.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:30.940
I really mean it,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:34.290
my housewares, my clothes, all my life.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.630
So I really took a shine
to her and her work.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.600
And now, she's here to tell us about it.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.268
Please welcome Alissa Bertrand.

00:00:42.268 --> 00:00:43.101
(audience applauds)

00:00:43.101 --> 00:00:44.018
- Hi, Drew!

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.690
- Alissa!
- I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.810
- Oh, I'm so thrilled.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.220
Okay, I am not kidding,

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.320
your work is exquisite.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.400
No wonder Vogue is all over it.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.624
It looks Vogue level!

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.070
You have six kids!
- Thank you.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.470
- Tell us about your models.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.180
- So yes, I'm a mom of six,
but on my page, Jabellafleur,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.150
you see my three younger girls,

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.900
which is Jayla, Jada, and Ella.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.730
And I design for them
because they still think

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.630
it's cool and fun to hang
with mom and take pictures

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.860
and to get on and move.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.850
- I mean, this really is, if
this was in the pages of Vogue,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.890
I would not bat an eye.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.850
It's really amazing what you are doing.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.740
And I heard that you liked
going to vintage thrift stores

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.050
rather than buying in regular stores.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.510
Why is that?

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.020
- Well, it started because, I mean,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.040
I always wanted to be a fashion designer,

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.970
but couldn't afford the
name brands and the logos,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.540
and plus, I couldn't
find prints that I liked.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.200
And I'm all about prints
and definitely florals,

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.573
the more the merrier.

00:01:53.592 --> 00:01:56.130
So I just started
repurposing and thrifting

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.870
and finding what I liked
to recreate for the girls.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.940
- What is your trick to photography?

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:06.260
Because, honestly, these
are not iPhone pics.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.550
I don't know what you're taking them on,

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:10.930
but they just look really elevated.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.010
- It is an iPhone. It's an XR.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.210
That's what I have.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.380
I mean, I'm keeping it simple.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.860
- It's an art. And I really am
amazed at what you're doing.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.940
Now, what are your top three
thrifting tips, please?

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:28.600
- Okay, so first, if you see
it and you like it, buy it

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.310
'cause it might not be there next time,

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:31.883
and that's a hard one to learn.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.130
Second is just go in and don't
expect to find something.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.350
If you're looking for a Jimi Hendrix,

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.540
and you look through 100
shirts and you didn't find it,

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.730
you're gonna probably come
out with something else

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.190
and still be okay.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:50.190
And then third, just go
in and search for you

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.400
and what you like and
what makes you feel good,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.370
rather than you going
to a department store

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:56.710
and it's being setup.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.900
Try something new.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.220
What's a $4 shirt that has patterns

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.040
when you're a neutral person?

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.120
Try it.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.930
Because the best thing is,
when you start thrifting,

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.530
it's fun and it can be
extremely rewarding.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:10.900
- I totally agree.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:14.660
As a lifelong thrifter and
vintage collector myself,

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.970
I just always find things I
could never find in a store.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.630
And I must say, your clothes
and pictures are no different.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.110
They're unique and one of a kind,

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.560
and we totally celebrate you.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.030
Thank you, Alissa, for being here.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:27.924
- Thank you so much!

00:03:27.924 --> 00:03:30.121
- Thank you so much
for coming on the show!

00:03:30.121 --> 00:03:32.788
(upbeat music)

